IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `oas-core`
IMPORT `oas-core-measures`
IMPORT `oas-core-periods`
IMPORT `oas-core-pension`
IMPORT `oa2-part2-amount`
IMPORT `oa2-part2-income`
IMPORT `oa2-part2-spouse`
IMPORT `oa2-part3-spouse-allowance`
IMPORT `oa2-seat`

-- Worked cases for oa2-seat: at least one for every question of the seat, with the facts a real person in the seat would
-- state, and the answer worked out by hand from the words of the section (the reasoning is in the comment on each case).
-- The same module rules are tested at length in the oa2-tests-* files; these cases test that the seat wires the answers
-- to the right rules. Where the encoding does not cover a case the question gives NOTHING (blank), and a case asserts it.
-- The cases are generated from a table of defaults and per-case changes (scratch/seat/cases_data.py in the working copy);
-- an input a case does not mention has the default value of the "everyday" scenario: the person is born March 15, 1960,
-- asks about September 2022, has lived in Canada for 40 years, is a citizen and has an approved application.


§ `Part II -- the Guaranteed Income Supplement`


§§ `Whether the Guaranteed Income Supplement can be paid to me (ss 10, 11)`

-- An everyday case: approved pension, an application made and approved, no bar: the supplement may be paid for September 2022.
#ASSERT `May I be paid the Guaranteed Income Supplement for this month` (YMD 2022 9 15) TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE (YMD 2022 9 1) FALSE FALSE NOTHING FALSE FALSE NOTHING FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- I have not applied, and nobody has waived or deemed my application (s 11(2)): not payable.
#ASSERT NOT `May I be paid the Guaranteed Income Supplement for this month` (YMD 2022 9 15) TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE (YMD 2022 9 1) FALSE FALSE NOTHING FALSE FALSE NOTHING FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- I have not applied, but the Minister waived the need when I turned 65 (s 11(3.1)): payable.
#ASSERT `May I be paid the Guaranteed Income Supplement for this month` (YMD 2022 9 15) TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE (YMD 2022 9 1) FALSE FALSE NOTHING FALSE FALSE NOTHING FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- A sponsor's undertaking is in effect (s 11(7)(e)): not payable.
#ASSERT NOT `May I be paid the Guaranteed Income Supplement for this month` (YMD 2022 9 15) TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE (YMD 2022 9 1) FALSE FALSE NOTHING FALSE FALSE NOTHING TRUE FALSE FALSE
-- A sponsor's undertaking is in effect, but an event under the regulations has occurred (s 11(8)(b)): payable.
#ASSERT `May I be paid the Guaranteed Income Supplement for this month` (YMD 2022 9 15) TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE (YMD 2022 9 1) FALSE FALSE NOTHING FALSE FALSE NOTHING TRUE FALSE TRUE
-- My pension application has not been approved, so I am not a pensioner (s 11(1)): not payable.
#ASSERT NOT `May I be paid the Guaranteed Income Supplement for this month` (YMD 2022 9 15) FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE (YMD 2022 9 1) FALSE FALSE NOTHING FALSE FALSE NOTHING FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- Out of Canada all of September 2022, having left in January 2022 (eight months): barred (s 11(7)(c)).
#ASSERT NOT `May I be paid the Guaranteed Income Supplement for this month` (YMD 2022 9 15) TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE (YMD 2022 9 1) FALSE TRUE (JUST (YMD 2022 1 20)) TRUE FALSE NOTHING FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- Same facts, asking about July 2022 (six months after leaving): not yet barred.
#ASSERT `May I be paid the Guaranteed Income Supplement for this month` (YMD 2022 7 31) TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE (YMD 2022 9 1) FALSE TRUE (JUST (YMD 2022 1 20)) TRUE FALSE NOTHING FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- Asking about August 2021 when my application month is September 2022: more than eleven months before (s 11(7)(a)): not payable.
#ASSERT NOT `May I be paid the Guaranteed Income Supplement for this month` (YMD 2021 8 15) TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE (YMD 2022 9 1) FALSE FALSE NOTHING FALSE FALSE NOTHING FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- Asking about October 2021: exactly eleven months before September 2022: payable.
#ASSERT `May I be paid the Guaranteed Income Supplement for this month` (YMD 2021 10 15) TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE (YMD 2022 9 1) FALSE FALSE NOTHING FALSE FALSE NOTHING FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- I applied in September 2022: the earliest month is eleven months before, October 2021 (s 11(7)(a)).
#ASSERT `In which month is the earliest for which a supplement can be paid to me` (YMD 2022 9 15) EQUALS (YMD 2021 10 1)
-- I applied on January 31, 2022: February 2021.
#ASSERT `In which month is the earliest for which a supplement can be paid to me` (YMD 2022 1 31) EQUALS (YMD 2021 2 1)
-- Born May 12, 1957: I turn 65 on May 12, 2022 and must file by the day before, May 11, 2022 (s 11(3.3)).
#ASSERT `By what day must I file a statement correcting inaccuracies` (YMD 1957 5 12) EQUALS (YMD 2022 5 11)
-- I told the Minister in writing on May 11, 2022, the day before I turned 65 (s 11(3.4)): in time.
#ASSERT `Did I decline the waiver in time` (YMD 1957 5 12) (YMD 2022 5 11)
-- I told the Minister on my 65th birthday: too late.
#ASSERT NOT `Did I decline the waiver in time` (YMD 1957 5 12) (YMD 2022 5 12)
-- I must apply from March 2023: the Minister may notify me not later than fifteen days before March 1, 2023: February 14, 2023 (s 11(5)).
#ASSERT `By what day may the Minister notify me that I must apply for later months` (YMD 2023 3 20) EQUALS (YMD 2023 2 14)

§§ `How much supplement (ss 12, 12.1)`

-- Quarter beginning October 1, 2005, previous maximum 600, index 102 against 100: 600 x 1.02 = 612 (s 12(2)).
#ASSERT `What is the maximum monthly supplement for a payment quarter` (YMD 2005 10 1) `s 12(1)(a): a person other than a person described in paragraph (b)` 600 102 100 NOTHING EQUALS (JUST 612)
-- The index fell (99 against 100): the maximum is never less than before (s 12(4)): 700.
#ASSERT `What is the maximum monthly supplement for a payment quarter` (YMD 2009 4 1) `s 12(1)(a): a person other than a person described in paragraph (b)` 700 99 100 NOTHING EQUALS (JUST 700)
-- NOT COVERED: a quarter that begins on or before June 30, 2005 is not one s 12(2) speaks to: the answer is blank, not zero.
#ASSERT `What is the maximum monthly supplement for a payment quarter` (YMD 2005 6 30) `s 12(1)(a): a person other than a person described in paragraph (b)` 562.93 101 100 NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
-- Maximum 1000, full pension 700, my pension 700, factor one, monthly base income 100: [(1000 + 700 - 700) x 1] - 100/2 = 950 (s 12(5)).
#ASSERT `How much supplement can I be paid for this month` (YMD 2022 9 15) 1000 700 700 700 700 40 FALSE FALSE TRUE 100 EQUALS 950
-- Monthly base income 3000: 1000 - 1500 is below zero: nothing is paid (fork F-12-2): 0.
#ASSERT `How much supplement can I be paid for this month` (YMD 2022 9 15) 1000 700 700 700 700 40 FALSE FALSE TRUE 3000 EQUALS 0
-- I have lived in Canada only 5 years since 18 and had no pension before 1996: factor 5/10: [(1000) x 0.5] - 50 = 450.
#ASSERT `How much supplement can I be paid for this month` (YMD 2022 9 15) 1000 700 700 700 700 5 FALSE FALSE TRUE 100 EQUALS 450
-- No spouse: one-twelfth of my 24,000 income: 2,000 (s 12(6)(a)).
#ASSERT `What is my monthly base income for the supplement` (YMD 2022 11 15) FALSE FALSE (YMD 2022 11 1) 24000 0 700 40 FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS 2000
-- A spouse with no pension payable: (12,000 + 12,000)/12 less the full pension 700, halved...: 650 (s 12(6)(b)).
#ASSERT `What is my monthly base income for the supplement` (YMD 2022 11 15) TRUE FALSE (YMD 2022 11 1) 12000 12000 700 40 FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS 650
-- A spouse whose pension starts in December 2022: for December itself the base income is 1,000 (s 12(6)(c)).
#ASSERT `What is my monthly base income for the supplement` (YMD 2022 12 1) TRUE TRUE (YMD 2022 12 20) 12000 12000 700 40 FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS 1000
-- No spouse, income 3,000, A = 50: the formula gives 30 (s 12.1(1)).
#ASSERT `How much may be added to my supplement under section 12.1(1)` (YMD 2011 8 1) 50 40 FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE 3000 0 EQUALS (JUST 30)
-- Income 5,000: the formula gives -12, and nothing negative is added: 0.
#ASSERT `How much may be added to my supplement under section 12.1(1)` (YMD 2011 8 1) 50 40 FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE 5000 0 EQUALS (JUST 0)
-- NOT COVERED: I have a spouse who is paid a benefit: 12.1(1) is silent (fork F-12.1-2): the answer is blank, not zero.
#ASSERT `How much may be added to my supplement under section 12.1(1)` (YMD 2011 8 1) 50 40 FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE 3000 8000 EQUALS NOTHING
-- A = 50, combined income 8,000: the formula gives 9 (s 12.1(2)).
#ASSERT `How much may be added to my supplement under section 12.1(2)` (YMD 2011 8 1) 50 40 FALSE FALSE TRUE 8000 EQUALS (JUST 9)
-- A = 35, combined income 8,000: the formula gives -6, so nothing is added: 0.
#ASSERT `How much may be added to my supplement under section 12.1(2)` (YMD 2011 8 1) 35 40 FALSE FALSE TRUE 8000 EQUALS (JUST 0)

§§ `My income, and the Minister's estimates (ss 13, 14)`

-- I am applying: I must state my income for the base calendar year (s 14(1)).
#ASSERT `Must I state my income for the base calendar year when I apply` TRUE
-- I am not applying: no duty under s 14(1).
#ASSERT NOT `Must I state my income for the base calendar year when I apply` FALSE
-- I stopped work in October 2022 and file on June 30, 2025, the last day (s 14(2)): I may.
#ASSERT `May I file a statement of estimated income because I stopped work` TRUE (YMD 2022 10 15) (YMD 2023 1 1) (YMD 2025 6 30)
-- One day later: too late.
#ASSERT NOT `May I file a statement of estimated income because I stopped work` TRUE (YMD 2022 10 15) (YMD 2023 1 1) (YMD 2025 7 1)
-- I am not an applicant and my spouse filed no statement: I may not.
#ASSERT NOT `May I file a statement of estimated income because I stopped work` FALSE (YMD 2022 10 15) (YMD 2023 1 1) (YMD 2025 6 30)
-- Stopped in October 2022: 2,000 over 2 months x 12 = 12,000, plus 3,000, plus 5,000 = 20,000 (s 14(2)).
#ASSERT `What income will be counted if I file a statement of estimated income` (YMD 2022 10 15) 2000 3000 5000 EQUALS (JUST 20000)
-- NOT COVERED: stopped in December, so there are no months left to divide by: the answer is blank, not zero.
#ASSERT `What income will be counted if I file a statement of estimated income` (YMD 2022 12 15) 2000 3000 5000 EQUALS NOTHING
-- My statement shows I stopped work in October 2022: payment from the month after, November 2022 (s 14(7)(a)).
#ASSERT `From which month can a supplement calculated on my statement be paid` `s 14(7)(a): the month in which the person ceased to hold an office or employment or ceased to carry on a business` (YMD 2022 10 15) EQUALS (YMD 2022 11 1)
-- My statement shows I lost pension income in October 2022: payment from October 2022 itself (s 14(7)(b)).
#ASSERT `From which month can a supplement calculated on my statement be paid` `s 14(7)(b): the month in which the person suffered the loss of income due to termination or reduction of pension income` (YMD 2022 10 15) EQUALS (YMD 2022 10 1)

§§ `My spouse or common-law partner (s 15)`

-- I am applying: I must say whether I have or had a spouse or common-law partner (s 15(1)).
#ASSERT `Must I say in my application whether I have or had a spouse or common-law partner` TRUE
-- I am not applying: no such duty.
#ASSERT NOT `Must I say in my application whether I have or had a spouse or common-law partner` FALSE
-- My application was waived, I had no spouse before and now I do: I must notify the Minister without delay (s 15(1.1)).
#ASSERT `Must I tell the Minister without delay that my situation has changed` TRUE TRUE TRUE
-- My application was not waived: no duty under s 15(1.1).
#ASSERT NOT `Must I tell the Minister without delay that my situation has changed` FALSE TRUE TRUE
-- I separate from my spouse: I must inform the Minister without delay (s 15(9)).
#ASSERT `Must I tell the Minister without delay if I separate or lose my spouse or partner` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- I had a spouse at the beginning of a month, and also the month before: nothing changed: no duty.
#ASSERT NOT `Must I tell the Minister without delay if I separate or lose my spouse or partner` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE
-- I had no spouse at the beginning of the previous month and have one now: I must inform the Minister (s 15(9)).
#ASSERT `Must I tell the Minister without delay if I separate or lose my spouse or partner` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE
-- Separated since January 2022, the Minister is satisfied: the supplement for May 2022 is worked out as though I had no spouse (s 15(4.1)).
#ASSERT `Will my supplement be worked out as though I had or had no spouse while we are separated` (YMD 2022 5 1) (YMD 2022 7 1) TRUE (YMD 2022 1 15) EQUALS (JUST `s 15: as though the person did not have a spouse or common-law partner on the last day of the previous payment period`)
-- NOT COVERED by (4.1): the month is before the months the subsection names: the answer is blank.
#ASSERT `Will my supplement be worked out as though I had or had no spouse while we are separated` (YMD 2022 4 30) (YMD 2022 7 1) TRUE (YMD 2022 1 15) EQUALS NOTHING
-- My common-law partner died in October 2022: from November 2022 the supplement is worked out as though I had no partner (s 15(7.2)).
#ASSERT `Will my supplement be worked out as though I had no partner after my common-law partner dies` (YMD 2022 11 1) (YMD 2022 9 1) TRUE (YMD 2022 10 15) EQUALS (JUST `s 15: as though the person did not have a spouse or common-law partner on the last day of the previous payment period`)
-- NOT COVERED: for October 2022, the month of the death itself, (7.2) does not apply: blank.
#ASSERT `Will my supplement be worked out as though I had no partner after my common-law partner dies` (YMD 2022 10 31) (YMD 2022 9 1) TRUE (YMD 2022 10 15) EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Decisions, notices and payment (ss 16 to 18.2)`

-- The Minister has my application: it must be considered without delay (s 16(1)).
#ASSERT `Must the Minister consider my application for the supplement without delay` TRUE FALSE
-- The Minister waived my need to apply: it must still be considered whether I am entitled (s 16(1)).
#ASSERT `Must the Minister consider my application for the supplement without delay` FALSE TRUE
-- No application received and no waiver: no duty yet.
#ASSERT NOT `Must the Minister consider my application for the supplement without delay` FALSE FALSE
-- I asked for particulars: the Minister must notify me in writing forthwith (s 16(2)).
#ASSERT `Will the Minister tell me in writing how my amount was worked out` TRUE
-- I have not asked: no duty to notify me of the basis.
#ASSERT NOT `Will the Minister tell me in writing how my amount was worked out` FALSE
-- The Minister decided no supplement may be paid to me: I must be told in writing, with reasons (s 16(2)).
#ASSERT `Will the Minister tell me in writing why no supplement may be paid to me` TRUE
-- No such decision: nothing to notify.
#ASSERT NOT `Will the Minister tell me in writing why no supplement may be paid to me` FALSE
-- Approved January 20, 2024; asking about March 2024: paid in arrears at the end of March (s 17).
#ASSERT `What is the earliest day on which payment for this month can be made` (YMD 2024 3 10) (YMD 2024 1 1) (YMD 2024 1 20) EQUALS (YMD 2024 3 31)
-- Same case: the latest day is also March 31.
#ASSERT `What is the latest day on which payment for this month can be made` (YMD 2024 3 10) (YMD 2024 1 1) (YMD 2024 1 20) EQUALS (YMD 2024 3 31)
-- Approved March 15, after the end of the first month payable: the payment for March (the month of approval) may be made at the end of March or of April: the latest is April 30.
#ASSERT `What is the latest day on which payment for this month can be made` (YMD 2024 3 10) (YMD 2024 1 1) (YMD 2024 3 15) EQUALS (YMD 2024 4 30)
-- The payment for February, a month before the month of approval: the earliest day is March 31.
#ASSERT `What is the earliest day on which payment for this month can be made` (YMD 2024 2 10) (YMD 2024 1 1) (YMD 2024 3 15) EQUALS (YMD 2024 3 31)
-- My actual income was 20,000 but I showed 10,000: I was paid 3,000 and would have been paid 2,400: 600 is deducted from later payments (s 18(a)).
#ASSERT `How much will be deducted from my later payments if my income was higher than I showed` 20000 10000 3000 2400 EQUALS 600
-- My actual income was lower than I showed: nothing is deducted.
#ASSERT `How much will be deducted from my later payments if my income was higher than I showed` 10000 20000 3000 2400 EQUALS 0
-- My actual income was 10,000 but I showed 20,000: I was paid 2,400 and should have been paid 3,000: 600 is paid to me (s 18(b), read as the mirror of (a)).
#ASSERT `How much will be paid to me if my income was lower than I showed` 10000 20000 2400 3000 EQUALS 600
-- My actual income was higher than I showed: nothing is paid to me under (b).
#ASSERT `How much will be paid to me if my income was lower than I showed` 20000 10000 2400 3000 EQUALS 0
-- The Minister approved my request in March 2024: the supplement stops on March 31 (s 18.1).
#ASSERT `On what day does my supplement stop if I ask the Minister to stop it` (YMD 2024 3 10) EQUALS (YMD 2024 3 31)
-- New application received in May 2024, and I chose September: it resumes in September 2024 (s 18.1).
#ASSERT `From which month can my supplement start again after I asked for it to stop` (YMD 2024 5 20) (YMD 2024 9 3) EQUALS (YMD 2024 9 1)
-- I chose April, before the new application: it resumes the month after receipt, June 2024.
#ASSERT `From which month can my supplement start again after I asked for it to stop` (YMD 2024 5 20) (YMD 2024 4 3) EQUALS (YMD 2024 6 1)
-- I asked for it to stop in March 2024 and it may resume in September: April is not payable (s 18.1).
#ASSERT NOT `Can my supplement still be paid for this month although I asked for it to stop` (YMD 2024 4 1) TRUE (YMD 2024 3 10) (JUST (YMD 2024 9 1))
-- September 2024, the month it may resume: payable again.
#ASSERT `Can my supplement still be paid for this month although I asked for it to stop` (YMD 2024 9 1) TRUE (YMD 2024 3 10) (JUST (YMD 2024 9 1))
-- I never asked for it to stop: payable.
#ASSERT `Can my supplement still be paid for this month although I asked for it to stop` (YMD 2024 4 1) FALSE (YMD 2024 3 10) (JUST (YMD 2024 9 1))
-- Payment began January 15, 2024; six months are allowed; I ask on July 15, 2024, the last day: I may (s 18.2(1)).
#ASSERT `May I ask for my supplement to be cancelled after payment has started` TRUE (YMD 2024 1 15) (YMD 2024 7 15)
-- One day later: too late.
#ASSERT NOT `May I ask for my supplement to be cancelled after payment has started` TRUE (YMD 2024 1 15) (YMD 2024 7 16)
-- The request is not made in writing: not made in the prescribed manner (Regulation 26.1(1)).
#ASSERT NOT `May I ask for my supplement to be cancelled after payment has started` FALSE (YMD 2024 1 15) (YMD 2024 7 15)

§ `Part III -- the Allowances, for a person 60 to 64`


§§ `Allowance for the spouse or common-law partner of a pensioner (ss 19, 20)`

-- An everyday case: a spouse of a pensioner, born March 15, 1960 (62), living with the pensioner, 25 years in Canada, joint application approved: the Allowance may be paid for September 2022.
#ASSERT `May I be paid an Allowance for this month as the spouse or common-law partner of a pensioner` (YMD 2022 9 15) `Spouse` FALSE FALSE FALSE NOTHING (YMD 1960 3 15) 25 TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE (YMD 2022 9 1) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE NOTHING FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (YMD 2000 7 1) FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE NOTHING NOTHING FALSE NOTHING
-- Born 1970, aged 52: too young (s 19(1)(b)).
#ASSERT NOT `May I be paid an Allowance for this month as the spouse or common-law partner of a pensioner` (YMD 2022 9 15) `Spouse` FALSE FALSE FALSE NOTHING (YMD 1970 3 15) 25 TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE (YMD 2022 9 1) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE NOTHING FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (YMD 2000 7 1) FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE NOTHING NOTHING FALSE NOTHING
-- Born 1950, aged 72: too old.
#ASSERT NOT `May I be paid an Allowance for this month as the spouse or common-law partner of a pensioner` (YMD 2022 9 15) `Spouse` FALSE FALSE FALSE NOTHING (YMD 1950 3 15) 25 TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE (YMD 2022 9 1) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE NOTHING FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (YMD 2000 7 1) FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE NOTHING NOTHING FALSE NOTHING
-- A sponsor's undertaking is in effect (s 19(6)(d)): not payable.
#ASSERT NOT `May I be paid an Allowance for this month as the spouse or common-law partner of a pensioner` (YMD 2022 9 15) `Spouse` FALSE FALSE FALSE NOTHING (YMD 1960 3 15) 25 TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE (YMD 2022 9 1) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE NOTHING FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE (YMD 2000 7 1) FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE NOTHING NOTHING FALSE NOTHING
-- A sponsor's undertaking, but an event under the regulations has occurred (s 19(6.2)): payable.
#ASSERT `May I be paid an Allowance for this month as the spouse or common-law partner of a pensioner` (YMD 2022 9 15) `Spouse` FALSE FALSE FALSE NOTHING (YMD 1960 3 15) 25 TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE (YMD 2022 9 1) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE NOTHING FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE (YMD 2000 7 1) FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE NOTHING NOTHING FALSE NOTHING
-- A spouse separated since January 2021: the separation condition of s 19(1)(a) is not met: not payable.
#ASSERT NOT `May I be paid an Allowance for this month as the spouse or common-law partner of a pensioner` (YMD 2022 9 15) `Spouse` TRUE FALSE FALSE (JUST (YMD 2021 1 1)) (YMD 1960 3 15) 25 TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE (YMD 2022 9 1) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE NOTHING FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (YMD 2000 7 1) FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE NOTHING NOTHING FALSE NOTHING
-- A former common-law partner who separated on July 15, 2022: payable (s 19(1)(a.1)).
#ASSERT `May I be paid an Allowance for this month as the spouse or common-law partner of a pensioner` (YMD 2022 9 15) `Former common-law partner` TRUE FALSE FALSE (JUST (YMD 2022 7 15)) (YMD 1960 3 15) 25 TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE (YMD 2022 9 1) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE NOTHING FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (YMD 2000 7 1) FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE NOTHING NOTHING FALSE NOTHING
-- Payment of my Allowance has not been approved: not payable (s 19(4)).
#ASSERT NOT `May I be paid an Allowance for this month as the spouse or common-law partner of a pensioner` (YMD 2022 9 15) `Spouse` FALSE FALSE FALSE NOTHING (YMD 1960 3 15) 25 TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (YMD 2022 9 1) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE NOTHING FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (YMD 2000 7 1) FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE NOTHING NOTHING FALSE NOTHING
-- I am serving a 400-day penitentiary sentence, incarcerated since March 2022 and not yet released: barred (s 19(6)(f)).
#ASSERT NOT `May I be paid an Allowance for this month as the spouse or common-law partner of a pensioner` (YMD 2022 9 15) `Spouse` FALSE FALSE FALSE NOTHING (YMD 1960 3 15) 25 TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE (YMD 2022 9 1) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE NOTHING FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (YMD 2000 7 1) TRUE TRUE 400 FALSE FALSE (JUST (YMD 2022 3 5)) NOTHING FALSE NOTHING
-- I must apply from March 2023: notice not later than February 14, 2023 (s 19(4.2)).
#ASSERT `By what day may the Minister notify me that I must apply for later months of the Allowance` (YMD 2023 3 20) EQUALS (YMD 2023 2 14)
-- The pensioner's income 4,800, mine 0: monthly joint income 400; pension equivalent 700, supplement equivalent 300, factor one: 700 (ss 19(7), 22(3)).
#ASSERT `How much Allowance may I be paid for this month as the spouse or common-law partner of a pensioner` (YMD 2022 9 15) 700 300 40 FALSE FALSE TRUE 4800 0 FALSE (YMD 2000 1 1) NOTHING FALSE FALSE (YMD 2000 1 1) EQUALS 700
-- A joint income of 100,000 a month: nothing is paid.
#ASSERT `How much Allowance may I be paid for this month as the spouse or common-law partner of a pensioner` (YMD 2022 9 15) 700 300 40 FALSE FALSE TRUE 1200000 0 FALSE (YMD 2000 1 1) NOTHING FALSE FALSE (YMD 2000 1 1) EQUALS 0
-- The pensioner is incarcerated (April 2023 is after the first month): only my income, 4,800 (400 a month), counts: 700.
#ASSERT `How much Allowance may I be paid for this month as the spouse or common-law partner of a pensioner` (YMD 2023 4 10) 700 300 40 FALSE FALSE TRUE 99999 4800 TRUE (YMD 2023 3 5) (JUST (YMD 2023 6 20)) FALSE FALSE (YMD 2000 1 1) EQUALS 700
-- I do not comply: the Minister may suspend payment (s 20).
#ASSERT `May payment of my Allowance be suspended if I do not comply with the Act` TRUE
-- I comply: no power to suspend.
#ASSERT NOT `May payment of my Allowance be suspended if I do not comply with the Act` FALSE
-- Suspended, and I now comply: payment may resume (s 20).
#ASSERT `May payment of my suspended Allowance be resumed` TRUE TRUE
-- Still not complying: not resumed.
#ASSERT NOT `May payment of my suspended Allowance be resumed` TRUE FALSE
-- I applied and the Minister is satisfied we live apart through no fault of ours: the Minister may direct (s 19(8)).
#ASSERT `May the Minister work out my Allowance without counting the pensioner's income` TRUE TRUE
-- I have not applied: no direction.
#ASSERT NOT `May the Minister work out my Allowance without counting the pensioner's income` FALSE TRUE

§§ `Allowance for a survivor (ss 21, 21.1)`

-- An everyday case: widowed in January 2020, born March 15, 1960 (62), 25 years in Canada, application approved: the survivor's Allowance may be paid for September 2022.
#ASSERT `May I be paid an Allowance for this month as a survivor` (YMD 2022 9 15) TRUE FALSE (YMD 2020 1 1) (YMD 1960 3 15) 25 TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE (YMD 2022 9 1) FALSE (YMD 2020 1 10) (YMD 2000 7 1) FALSE NOTHING FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE NOTHING NOTHING FALSE
-- My spouse has not died: I am not a survivor (s 21(1)).
#ASSERT NOT `May I be paid an Allowance for this month as a survivor` (YMD 2022 9 15) FALSE FALSE (YMD 2020 1 1) (YMD 1960 3 15) 25 TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE (YMD 2022 9 1) FALSE (YMD 2020 1 10) (YMD 2000 7 1) FALSE NOTHING FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE NOTHING NOTHING FALSE
-- I have since become the spouse of another person: no longer a survivor.
#ASSERT NOT `May I be paid an Allowance for this month as a survivor` (YMD 2022 9 15) TRUE TRUE (YMD 2020 1 1) (YMD 1960 3 15) 25 TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE (YMD 2022 9 1) FALSE (YMD 2020 1 10) (YMD 2000 7 1) FALSE NOTHING FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE NOTHING NOTHING FALSE
-- Born 1970, aged 52: too young (s 21(1)(a)).
#ASSERT NOT `May I be paid an Allowance for this month as a survivor` (YMD 2022 9 15) TRUE FALSE (YMD 2020 1 1) (YMD 1970 3 15) 25 TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE (YMD 2022 9 1) FALSE (YMD 2020 1 10) (YMD 2000 7 1) FALSE NOTHING FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE NOTHING NOTHING FALSE
-- A sponsor's undertaking is in effect (s 21(9)(c)): not payable.
#ASSERT NOT `May I be paid an Allowance for this month as a survivor` (YMD 2022 9 15) TRUE FALSE (YMD 2020 1 1) (YMD 1960 3 15) 25 TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE (YMD 2022 9 1) FALSE (YMD 2020 1 10) (YMD 2000 7 1) FALSE NOTHING FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE NOTHING NOTHING FALSE
-- A sponsor's undertaking, but an event under the regulations has occurred (s 21(9.1)): payable.
#ASSERT `May I be paid an Allowance for this month as a survivor` (YMD 2022 9 15) TRUE FALSE (YMD 2020 1 1) (YMD 1960 3 15) 25 TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE (YMD 2022 9 1) FALSE (YMD 2020 1 10) (YMD 2000 7 1) FALSE NOTHING FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE NOTHING NOTHING FALSE
-- A 400-day penitentiary sentence, incarcerated since March 2022 and not released: barred (s 21(9)(d)).
#ASSERT NOT `May I be paid an Allowance for this month as a survivor` (YMD 2022 9 15) TRUE FALSE (YMD 2020 1 1) (YMD 1960 3 15) 25 TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE (YMD 2022 9 1) FALSE (YMD 2020 1 10) (YMD 2000 7 1) FALSE NOTHING FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE 400 FALSE FALSE (JUST (YMD 2022 3 5)) NOTHING FALSE
-- Widowed January 2020, turned 60 in March 2020: the later is March; the Allowance may be paid from April 2020 (s 21(6)).
#ASSERT `From which month may a survivor's Allowance be paid to me` (YMD 2020 1 15) (YMD 1960 3 15) EQUALS (YMD 2020 4 1)
-- Widowed June 2021, after turning 60: from July 2021.
#ASSERT `From which month may a survivor's Allowance be paid to me` (YMD 2021 6 20) (YMD 1960 3 15) EQUALS (YMD 2021 7 1)
-- I must apply from March 2023: notice not later than February 14, 2023 (s 21(5.2)).
#ASSERT `By what day may the Minister notify me that I must apply for later months of the survivor's Allowance` (YMD 2023 3 20) EQUALS (YMD 2023 2 14)
-- Pension equivalent 700, survivor's supplement equivalent 454.09, factor one, income 4,800 (400 a month): 854.09 (ss 21(10), 22(4)).
#ASSERT `How much Allowance may I be paid for this month as a survivor` (YMD 2022 9 15) 700 454.09 40 FALSE FALSE TRUE 4800 EQUALS 854.09
-- No income: 700 + 454.09 = 1,154.09.
#ASSERT `How much Allowance may I be paid for this month as a survivor` (YMD 2022 9 15) 700 454.09 40 FALSE FALSE TRUE 0 EQUALS 1154.09
-- A very high income: nothing is paid.
#ASSERT `How much Allowance may I be paid for this month as a survivor` (YMD 2022 9 15) 700 454.09 40 FALSE FALSE TRUE 1200000 EQUALS 0
-- The Minister is informed and satisfied that I was convicted of murder of my spouse: not payable (s 21.1(1)).
#ASSERT `Is a survivor's Allowance not payable to me because of a conviction` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- No such conviction: payable.
#ASSERT NOT `Is a survivor's Allowance not payable to me because of a conviction` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- Convicted of manslaughter and released on a probation order: s 21.1 does not apply (s 21.1(8)).
#ASSERT NOT `Is a survivor's Allowance not payable to me because of a conviction` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE
-- The conviction was reversed and all appeals are exhausted: payable (s 21.1(2)).
#ASSERT NOT `Is a survivor's Allowance not payable to me because of a conviction` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE
-- The conviction was reversed but an appeal is open: still not payable.
#ASSERT `Is a survivor's Allowance not payable to me because of a conviction` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE
-- I received an Allowance and am found convicted: I am deemed not to have been entitled and the Minister must recover it (s 21.1(4)).
#ASSERT `Must I repay an Allowance I received if I am found to have been convicted` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- I received nothing: nothing to recover.
#ASSERT NOT `Must I repay an Allowance I received if I am found to have been convicted` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- Something was recovered from me and the conviction is reversed with all appeals exhausted: it must be repaid (s 21.1(2)).
#ASSERT `Will the Minister repay what was recovered from me if my conviction is reversed` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE
-- The conviction stands: nothing to repay.
#ASSERT NOT `Will the Minister repay what was recovered from me if my conviction is reversed` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE

§§ `The supplement and the top-up that go with the Allowance (ss 22, 22.1)`

-- My spouse's Allowance application was approved: my supplement is paid under s 22(2) instead of Part II.
#ASSERT `Will I be paid a supplement under section 22(2) instead of under Part II` TRUE FALSE
-- The requirement for that application was waived: the same.
#ASSERT `Will I be paid a supplement under section 22(2) instead of under Part II` FALSE TRUE
-- No application for my spouse and no waiver: the Part II supplement applies.
#ASSERT NOT `Will I be paid a supplement under section 22(2) instead of under Part II` FALSE FALSE
-- My spouse's application was approved: I am treated as having applied and been approved for the Part II supplement (s 22(7)).
#ASSERT `Am I treated as having applied for the supplement under Part II` TRUE
-- No approved application: no deeming.
#ASSERT NOT `Am I treated as having applied for the supplement under Part II` FALSE
-- My spouse's Allowance is suspended: I may be paid the Part II supplement for the month (s 22(5)).
#ASSERT `May I be paid the Part II supplement again while my spouse's or partner's Allowance is suspended or has ended` TRUE FALSE
-- Neither suspended nor terminated: no.
#ASSERT NOT `May I be paid the Part II supplement again while my spouse's or partner's Allowance is suspended or has ended` FALSE FALSE
-- Allowance to my spouse 300, supplement under Part III 200, under Part II 600: 300 (s 22(6)).
#ASSERT `How much supplement may I be paid for the month when my spouse or partner is paid an Allowance` 300 200 600 EQUALS (JUST 300)
-- NOT COVERED: the amounts fit none of the cases s 22(6) states: blank.
#ASSERT `How much supplement may I be paid for the month when my spouse or partner is paid an Allowance` 400 200 600 EQUALS NOTHING
-- A = 35, combined income 6,000, 40 years in Canada: 15 may be added (s 22.1(2)).
#ASSERT `How much may be added to my Allowance as the spouse or common-law partner of a pensioner` (YMD 2012 1 1) 35 40 FALSE FALSE TRUE 6000 EQUALS 15
-- Only 5 years in Canada: the formula gives -2.5, so nothing is added: 0.
#ASSERT `How much may be added to my Allowance as the spouse or common-law partner of a pensioner` (YMD 2012 1 1) 35 5 FALSE FALSE TRUE 6000 EQUALS 0
-- A = 50, income 3,000, 40 years in Canada: 30 may be added (s 22.1(3)).
#ASSERT `How much may be added to my Allowance as a survivor` (YMD 2012 1 1) 50 40 FALSE FALSE TRUE 3000 EQUALS 30

§§ `When an Allowance starts, and how it is paid (ss 23 to 26)`

-- Approved March 10, 2024: payment starts in the first month after, April 2024 (s 23(1)).
#ASSERT `In which month does payment of my Allowance start` (YMD 2024 3 10) EQUALS (YMD 2024 4 1)
-- Approved December 20, 2024: January 2025.
#ASSERT `In which month does payment of my Allowance start` (YMD 2024 12 20) EQUALS (YMD 2025 1 1)
-- Received March 5 and approved April 10 (after the month I applied): the prescribed earlier date March 20 is not before March 5: it may be effective from March 20 (s 23(1)).
#ASSERT `Can my approval be made effective from an earlier date` (YMD 2024 3 5) (YMD 2024 4 10) (JUST (YMD 2024 3 20)) EQUALS (JUST (YMD 2024 3 20))
-- NOT COVERED: approved March 31, the last day of the month I applied, not after it: blank.
#ASSERT `Can my approval be made effective from an earlier date` (YMD 2024 3 5) (YMD 2024 3 31) (JUST (YMD 2024 3 20)) EQUALS NOTHING
-- Waived in September 2022: payment may not start before October 2021, eleven months earlier (s 23(1.1)).
#ASSERT `How far back may payment of my Allowance start if the Minister waived my application` (YMD 2022 9 15) EQUALS (YMD 2021 10 1)
-- Turned 60 on March 15, 2020; applied September 10, 2022: the later of a year before (September 10, 2021) and my 60th birthday: September 10, 2021 (s 23(2)).
#ASSERT `How far back may my approval be made effective if I applied after turning 60` (YMD 1960 3 15) (YMD 2022 9 10) EQUALS (JUST (YMD 2021 9 10))
-- Applied April 1, 2020: a year before is before my 60th birthday: March 15, 2020.
#ASSERT `How far back may my approval be made effective if I applied after turning 60` (YMD 1960 3 15) (YMD 2020 4 1) EQUALS (JUST (YMD 2020 3 15))
-- NOT COVERED: I applied before turning 60: blank.
#ASSERT `How far back may my approval be made effective if I applied after turning 60` (YMD 1960 3 15) (YMD 2019 1 1) EQUALS NOTHING
-- Approved while I am incarcerated, I notified the Minister and remain eligible: payment starts in the month of my release (s 23(3)).
#ASSERT `Does my Allowance start in the month I am released from prison` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE
-- I did not notify the Minister: it does not start.
#ASSERT NOT `Does my Allowance start in the month I am released from prison` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE
-- The Minister has my application: it must be considered without delay (s 24(1)).
#ASSERT `Must the Minister consider my application for an Allowance without delay` TRUE FALSE
-- No application received and no waiver: no duty yet.
#ASSERT NOT `Must the Minister consider my application for an Allowance without delay` FALSE FALSE
-- I asked for particulars: the Minister must notify me forthwith in writing (s 24(2)).
#ASSERT `Will the Minister tell me in writing how the amount of my Allowance was worked out` TRUE
-- I have not asked: no duty.
#ASSERT NOT `Will the Minister tell me in writing how the amount of my Allowance was worked out` FALSE
-- The Minister decided no Allowance may be paid: I must be told in writing, with reasons (s 24(2)).
#ASSERT `Will the Minister tell me in writing why no Allowance may be paid to me` TRUE
-- No such decision.
#ASSERT NOT `Will the Minister tell me in writing why no Allowance may be paid to me` FALSE
-- Approved January 20, 2024; asking about March 2024: paid in arrears at the end of March (s 25).
#ASSERT `What is the earliest day on which my Allowance for this month can be paid` (YMD 2024 3 10) (YMD 2024 1 1) (YMD 2024 1 20) EQUALS (YMD 2024 3 31)
-- Same case: the latest is also March 31.
#ASSERT `What is the latest day on which my Allowance for this month can be paid` (YMD 2024 3 10) (YMD 2024 1 1) (YMD 2024 1 20) EQUALS (YMD 2024 3 31)
-- Approved March 15, after the end of the first month payable: the payment for March may be made by April 30.
#ASSERT `What is the latest day on which my Allowance for this month can be paid` (YMD 2024 3 10) (YMD 2024 1 1) (YMD 2024 3 15) EQUALS (YMD 2024 4 30)
-- The payment for February, approved on March 15: the earliest is March 31.
#ASSERT `What is the earliest day on which my Allowance for this month can be paid` (YMD 2024 2 10) (YMD 2024 1 1) (YMD 2024 3 15) EQUALS (YMD 2024 3 31)
-- I already gave the information for the supplement: the Minister may waive it for the Allowance (s 26(1.1)).
#ASSERT `May the Minister waive my having to file information again for the Allowance` TRUE
-- I did not: no waiver.
#ASSERT NOT `May the Minister waive my having to file information again for the Allowance` FALSE
